  "plan": {
    "goal": "Recapitulate physiological arterial wall shear stress in an endothelial-lined microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "HUVEC physiological shear range is 0.1–1.0 Pa (vasculature convention). Arterial endothelium experiences shear at the upper end of this range (~1 Pa), so 1.0 Pa was chosen as the target. A 400 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm channel at 40 µL/min yields 1.0 Pa wall shear stress (τ = 6·μ·Q/(w·h²)). The flow is laminar (Re ≈ 2.7), the pressure drop is negligible (~0.4 kPa), and the 1.2 s residence time is appropriate for a single-pass arterial channel. HUVEC seeding density 1–2×10⁴ cells/cm² per registry.",
